**What you should see**

Once the folder is open, the Explorer sidebar shows the folder name at the top, with a tree of all files and subfolders beneath it. You should see your `.tsmap`, `.tsvar`, and `.md` files listed. If Docs Assembler is installed, these files will have their own icons and syntax highlighting.

> **Note:** If you open a single file instead of a folder, VS Code opens it in **restricted mode**. Many extensions, including Docs Assembler, will not work fully because they cannot see the rest of your project. If your maps and variables are not being recognised, check that you have opened the folder, not just a file.

